1
00:00:03,339 --> 00:00:09,258
Chapter 22 Mr. Rochester had given me but one week's leave

2
00:00:09,260 --> 00:00:13,660
of absence, yet a month elapsed before I quitted Gateshead.

3
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:19,900
I wished to leave immediately after the funeral, but Georgiano entreated me to

4
00:00:19,900 --> 00:00:25,279
stay till she could get off to London, with her she was now at last invited by

5
00:00:25,281 --> 00:00:29,569
her uncle, Mr. Gibson, who had come down to direct

6
00:00:29,571 --> 00:00:33,120
his sister's internment and settle the family affairs.

7
00:00:34,559 --> 00:00:38,680
Georgiana said she dreaded being left alone with Eliza.

8
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:44,400
From her, she got neither sympathy in her dejection, support in her fears,

9
00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:46,540
nor aid in her preparations.

10
00:00:47,599 --> 00:00:53,139
So I bore with her feeble minded wailings and selfish lamentations as well as I

11
00:00:53,141 --> 00:00:57,639
could and did my best in sowing for her and packing her dresses.

12
00:00:58,980 --> 00:01:06,980
It is true that while I worked she would idle and I thought to myself, if you and I

13
00:01:06,980 --> 00:01:10,555
were destined to live always together cousin, we

14
00:01:10,557 --> 00:01:13,440
would commence matters on a different footing.

15
00:01:14,059 --> 00:01:18,160
I should not settle tamedly down into being the forbearing party.

16
00:01:19,260 --> 00:01:24,139
I should assign you your share of labour and compel you to accomplish it,

17
00:01:24,699 --> 00:01:27,239
or else it should be left undone.

18
00:01:27,819 --> 00:01:32,076
I should insist, also, on you're keeping some of those

19
00:01:32,078 --> 00:01:36,519
drooling, half insincere complaints hushed in your own breast.

20
00:01:37,720 --> 00:01:43,120
It is only because our connection happens to be very transitory and comes at a

21
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:46,349
peculiarly mournful season that I consent thus

22
00:01:46,349 --> 00:01:50,400
to render it so patient and compliant on my part.

23
00:01:51,819 --> 00:01:55,398
At last I saw Georgiana off, but now it was

24
00:01:55,398 --> 00:01:59,161
Eliza's turn to request me to stay another week.

25
00:01:59,779 --> 00:02:03,080
Her plans required all her time and attention, she said.

26
00:02:03,879 --> 00:02:09,500
She was about to depart for some unknown born, and all day long she stayed in her

27
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:14,879
own room, her door bolted within, filling trunks, emptying drawers,

28
00:02:15,160 --> 00:02:18,339
burning papers and holding no communication with anyone.

29
00:02:19,160 --> 00:02:24,940
She wished me to look after the house, to see callers and answer notes of condolence.

30
00:02:25,279 --> 00:02:27,940
One morning she told me I was at liberty.

31
00:02:29,260 --> 00:02:36,360
And she added, I am obliged to you for your valuable services and discrete conduct.

32
00:02:37,059 --> 00:02:42,000
There is some difference between living with such and one as you and with Georgiana.

33
00:02:42,699 --> 00:02:46,139
You perform your own part in life and burden no one.

34
00:02:47,580 --> 00:02:52,540
Tomorrow she continued, I set out for the continent.

35
00:02:53,480 --> 00:02:55,813
I shall take up my abode in a religious house

36
00:02:55,813 --> 00:02:59,281
near Lille, a nunnery you would call it.

37
00:02:59,360 --> 00:03:01,839
There I shall be quiet and unmolested.

38
00:03:02,599 --> 00:03:07,760
I shall devote myself for a time to the examination of the Roman Catholic dogmas,

39
00:03:08,760 --> 00:03:11,680
and to a careful study of the workings of their system.

40
00:03:12,519 --> 00:03:18,076
If I find it to be, as I half suspect it is, the one best

41
00:03:18,078 --> 00:03:23,319
calculated to ensure the doing of all things decently and in order.

42
00:03:24,599 --> 00:03:28,220
I shall embrace the tenets of Rome and probably take the veil.

43
00:03:29,459 --> 00:03:34,800
I neither express surprise at this resolution nor attempted to dissuade her from it.

44
00:03:35,440 --> 00:03:38,319
The vocation will fit you to a hair, I thought.

45
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:40,500
Much good may it do you.

46
00:03:41,639 --> 00:03:45,699
When we parted, she said, goodbye cousin Jane Eyre.

47
00:03:46,379 --> 00:03:47,379
I wish you well.

48
00:03:47,680 --> 00:03:48,680
You have some sense.

49
00:03:49,260 --> 00:03:50,260
I then returned.

50
00:03:50,580 --> 00:03:52,760
You are not without sense, cousin Eliza.

51
00:03:53,319 --> 00:03:56,118
But what you have, I suppose, in another year,

52
00:03:56,118 --> 00:03:59,561
will be walled up alive in a French convent.

53
00:04:00,180 --> 00:04:03,779
However, it is not my business, and so it suits you.

54
00:04:04,220 --> 00:04:05,220
I don't much care.

55
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:08,300
You are in the right, said she.

56
00:04:09,160 --> 00:04:12,239
And with these words, we each went our separate way.

57
00:04:13,680 --> 00:04:18,139
As I shall not have occasion to refer either to her or her sister again,

58
00:04:18,879 --> 00:04:25,279
I may as well mention here that Georgiana made an advantageous match with a wealthy

59
00:04:25,281 --> 00:04:32,160
worn -out man of fashion and that Eliza actually took the veil and is at this day

60
00:04:32,161 --> 00:04:36,366
superior of the convent where she passed the period of

61
00:04:36,368 --> 00:04:40,000
her novitiate and which she endowed with her fortune.

62
00:04:40,779 --> 00:04:46,540
How people feel when they are returning home from an absence long or short,

63
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:48,160
I did not know.

64
00:04:48,660 --> 00:04:51,559
I had never experienced the sensation.

65
00:04:52,660 --> 00:04:58,699
I had known what it was to come back to Gateshead, when a child after a long walk,

66
00:04:59,440 --> 00:05:04,959
to be scolded for looking cold or gloomy, and later, what it was to come back from

67
00:05:04,961 --> 00:05:08,574
church to lowered, to long for a plentiest meal

68
00:05:08,576 --> 00:05:12,421
and a good fire, and to be unable to get either.

69
00:05:12,639 --> 00:05:15,500
Neither of these returning was very pleasant or desirable.

70
00:05:16,300 --> 00:05:19,315
No magnet drew me to a given point, increasing

71
00:05:19,315 --> 00:05:22,459
in its strength of attraction the nearer I came.

72
00:05:23,419 --> 00:05:26,260
The return to Thornfield was yet to be tried.

73
00:05:27,440 --> 00:05:34,000
My journey seemed tedious, very tedious, 50 miles one day, a night spent at an inn,

74
00:05:34,519 --> 00:05:36,279
50 miles the next day.

75
00:05:36,760 --> 00:05:40,760
During the first 12 hours, I thought of Mrs. Reed in her last moments.

76
00:05:41,540 --> 00:05:47,139
I saw her disfigured and discolored face, and heard her strangely altered voice.

77
00:05:47,860 --> 00:05:53,519
I mused on the funeral day, the coffin, the hearse, the black train of tenants and

78
00:05:53,521 --> 00:05:58,919
servants, few as the number of relatives, the gaping vault, the silent church,

79
00:05:59,500 --> 00:06:00,500
the solemn service.

80
00:06:01,339 --> 00:06:04,199
Then I thought of Eliza and Georgiana.

81
00:06:04,919 --> 00:06:11,220
I beheld one, the sinister of a ballroom, the other, the inmate of a convent cell,

82
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:16,720
and I dwelt on and analysed their separate peculiarities of person and character.

83
00:06:17,639 --> 00:06:22,660
The evening arrival at the great town of ahhh scattered these thoughts.

84
00:06:23,639 --> 00:06:26,220
Night gave them quite another turn.

85
00:06:27,180 --> 00:06:31,959
Layed down on my traveller's bed, I left reminiscence for anticipation.

86
00:06:33,199 --> 00:06:38,260
I was going back to Thornfield, but how long was I to stay there?

87
00:06:39,099 --> 00:06:40,099
Not long.

88
00:06:40,699 --> 00:06:42,099
Of that I was sure.

89
00:06:43,160 --> 00:06:46,639
I had heard from Mrs. Fairfax in the interim of my absence.

90
00:06:47,580 --> 00:06:49,519
The party at the hall was dispersed.

91
00:06:50,580 --> 00:06:53,769
Mr. Rochester had left for London three weeks ago,

92
00:06:53,771 --> 00:06:57,099
but he was then expected to return in a fortnight.

93
00:06:58,139 --> 00:07:03,160
Mrs. Fairfax surmised that he was gone to make arrangements for his wedding,

94
00:07:03,660 --> 00:07:05,940
as he had talked of purchasing a new carriage.

95
00:07:06,699 --> 00:07:11,139
She said the idea of his marrying Mrs. Ingram still seemed strange to her.

96
00:07:12,040 --> 00:07:17,360
But from what everybody said, and from what she had herself seen, she could no

97
00:07:17,360 --> 00:07:20,120
longer doubt that the event would shortly take place.

98
00:07:21,019 --> 00:07:25,959
You would be strangely incredulous if you did doubt it, was my mental comment.

99
00:07:26,800 --> 00:07:27,860
I don't doubt it.

100
00:07:28,760 --> 00:07:29,900
The question followed.

101
00:07:30,779 --> 00:07:32,160
Where was I to go?

102
00:07:33,260 --> 00:07:36,099
I dreamt of Mrs. Ingram all the night.

103
00:07:36,101 --> 00:07:39,949
In a vivid morning dream, I saw her closing the gates of

104
00:07:39,951 --> 00:07:43,239
Thornfield against me and pointing me out another road.

105
00:07:44,120 --> 00:07:49,459
And Mr. Rochester looked on with his arms folded, smiling sardónically as it seemed,

106
00:07:49,900 --> 00:07:51,800
at both her and me.

107
00:07:53,080 --> 00:07:57,360
I had not notified to Mrs. Fairfax the exact day of my return.

108
00:07:58,239 --> 00:08:02,300
For I did not wish either car or carriage to meet me at Milkot.

109
00:08:03,819 --> 00:08:10,980
I proposed to walk the distance quietly by myself and very quietly after leaving my

110
00:08:10,980 --> 00:08:16,839
box in the Oslo's care, did I slip away from the George Inn about six o'clock of a

111
00:08:16,841 --> 00:08:23,080
June evening and take the old road to Thornfield, a road which lay chiefly

112
00:08:23,080 --> 00:08:26,480
through fields and was now little frequented.

113
00:08:27,180 --> 00:08:31,879
It was not a bright or splendid summer evening, though fair and soft.

114
00:08:32,900 --> 00:08:38,599
The haymakers were at work all along the road, and the sky, though far from

115
00:08:38,601 --> 00:08:41,940
cloudless, was such as promised well for the future.

116
00:08:42,779 --> 00:08:46,703
Its blue, where blue was visible, was mild and

117
00:08:46,703 --> 00:08:50,040
settled, and its clouds strut a high and thin.

118
00:08:50,669 --> 00:08:52,440
The west, too, was warm.

119
00:08:53,260 --> 00:08:55,199
No watery gleam chilled it.

120
00:08:55,819 --> 00:09:00,620
It seemed as if there was a fire lit, an altar burning behind its screen of

121
00:09:00,620 --> 00:09:05,300
marbled vapor, and out of apertures shone a golden redness.

122
00:09:06,339 --> 00:09:12,339
I felt glad as the road shortened before me, so glad that I stopped once to ask

123
00:09:12,341 --> 00:09:18,019
myself what that joy meant, and to remind reason that it was not to my home I was

124
00:09:18,021 --> 00:09:22,235
going, or to a permanent resting place, or to a place where

125
00:09:22,237 --> 00:09:26,440
fond friends looked out for me, and waited my arrival.

126
00:09:27,959 --> 00:09:34,379
Mrs. Fairfax will smile you a calm welcome to be sure, said I, and little Adele will

127
00:09:34,381 --> 00:09:38,860
clap her hands and jump to see you, but you know very well you are thinking of

128
00:09:38,860 --> 00:09:42,720
another than they, and that he is not thinking of you.

129
00:09:43,900 --> 00:09:49,860
But what is so headstrong as youth, what so blind as inexperience,

130
00:09:50,160 --> 00:09:56,260
these affirmed that it was pleasure enough to have the privilege of again looking on

131
00:09:56,260 --> 00:10:03,059
Mr. Rochester, whether he looked on me or not, and they added, hasten, hasten,

132
00:10:03,459 --> 00:10:06,353
be with him while you may, but a few more days or

133
00:10:06,353 --> 00:10:09,300
weeks at most, and you are parted from him forever.

134
00:10:10,739 --> 00:10:15,900
And then I strangled a newborn agony, a deformed thing which I could not

135
00:10:15,900 --> 00:10:19,239
persuade myself to own and rear, and ran on.

136
00:10:20,199 --> 00:10:26,660
They are making hay too in thornfield meadows, or rather the laborers are just

137
00:10:26,661 --> 00:10:30,580
quitting their work and returning home with their rakes on their shoulders.

138
00:10:31,639 --> 00:10:36,894
Now, at the hour I arrive, I have but a field or two to

139
00:10:36,896 --> 00:10:40,919
traverse, and then I shall cross the road and reach the gates.

140
00:10:42,080 --> 00:10:47,239
How full the hedges are of roses, but I have no time to gather any.

141
00:10:48,059 --> 00:10:49,160
I want to be at the house.

142
00:10:50,059 --> 00:10:54,519
I passed a tall briar, shooting leafy and flowery branches across the path.

143
00:10:55,540 --> 00:11:01,599
I see the narrow style with stone steps, and I see Mr. Rochester sitting there,

144
00:11:02,279 --> 00:11:03,739
a book and a pencil in his hand.

145
00:11:04,339 --> 00:11:05,339
He is writing.

146
00:11:06,360 --> 00:11:11,180
Well, he is not a ghost, yet every nerve I have is unstrung.

147
00:11:12,040 --> 00:11:14,860
For a moment, I am beyond my own mastery.

148
00:11:16,180 --> 00:11:17,180
What does it mean?

149
00:11:18,360 --> 00:11:21,425
I did not think I should tremble in this way when I saw him,

150
00:11:21,425 --> 00:11:23,879
or lose my voice or the power of motion in his presence.

151
00:11:24,699 --> 00:11:26,580
I will go back as soon as I can stir.

152
00:11:27,180 --> 00:11:30,500
I need not make an absolute fool of myself.

153
00:11:31,379 --> 00:11:32,660
I know another way to the house.

154
00:11:33,680 --> 00:11:37,519
It does not signify if I knew twenty ways for he has seen me.

155
00:11:39,279 --> 00:11:43,819
Hello, he cries, and he puts up his book and his pencil.

156
00:11:44,599 --> 00:11:45,139
There you are.

157
00:11:45,519 --> 00:11:46,519
Come on, if you please.

158
00:11:47,900 --> 00:11:53,279
I suppose I do come on, though in what fashion I know not, being scarcely

159
00:11:53,281 --> 00:11:57,339
cognizant of my movements, and solicit us only to appear calm.

160
00:11:58,160 --> 00:12:03,940
And above all, to control the working muscles of my face, which I feel rebel,

161
00:12:04,300 --> 00:12:09,300
insolently against my will, and struggle to express what I had resolved to conceal.

162
00:12:10,120 --> 00:12:12,540
But I have a veil, it is down.

163
00:12:13,379 --> 00:12:16,519
I may make shift yet to behave with decent composure.

164
00:12:17,680 --> 00:12:19,319
And this is Jane Eyre.

165
00:12:19,900 --> 00:12:22,040
Are you coming from Millcoat and on foot?

166
00:12:22,819 --> 00:12:29,160
Yes, just one of your tricks, not to send for a carriage, and come clattering over

167
00:12:29,161 --> 00:12:34,500
street and road like a common mortal, but to steal into the vicinage of your

168
00:12:34,500 --> 00:12:38,860
home along with twilight, just as if you were a dream or a shade.

169
00:12:39,580 --> 00:12:42,440
What the deuce have you done with yourself this last month?

170
00:12:43,720 --> 00:12:46,080
I have been with my aunt, sir.

171
00:12:46,519 --> 00:12:47,519
Who is dead?

172
00:12:48,519 --> 00:12:50,839
A true Janian reply.

173
00:12:51,699 --> 00:12:53,599
Good angels be my God.

174
00:12:54,379 --> 00:12:58,839
She comes from the other world, from the abode of people who are dead,

175
00:12:59,699 --> 00:13:03,040
and tells me so when she meets me alone here in the gloaming.

176
00:13:03,819 --> 00:13:10,000
If I dead I'd touch you to see if you are substance or shadow you elf, but I'd as

177
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:13,540
soon offer to take hold of a blue igneus fatuous light in a marsh.

178
00:13:14,239 --> 00:13:18,739
Truant, truant, he added, when he had paused an instant.

179
00:13:19,739 --> 00:13:24,300
Absent from me a whole month and forgetting me quite, I'll be sworn.

180
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:31,959
I knew there would be pleasure in meeting my master again, even though broken by the

181
00:13:31,961 --> 00:13:35,277
fear that he was so soon to cease to be my master,

182
00:13:35,279 --> 00:13:38,341
and by the knowledge that I was nothing to him.

183
00:13:39,080 --> 00:13:45,180
But there was ever in Mr. Rochester, so at least I thought, such a wealth of

184
00:13:45,180 --> 00:13:50,319
the power of communicating happiness, that to taste but of the crumbs he

185
00:13:50,321 --> 00:13:55,860
scattered to stray and stranger birds like me, was to feast genially.

186
00:13:56,739 --> 00:13:58,620
His last words were balm.

187
00:13:59,559 --> 00:14:04,961
They seemed to imply that it imported something to him, whether I forgot him or not.

188
00:14:05,180 --> 00:14:10,639
And he had spoken of Thornfield as my home, would that it were my home.

189
00:14:11,559 --> 00:14:15,500
He did not leave the style, and I hardly like to ask to go by.

190
00:14:16,720 --> 00:14:19,500
I inquired soon if he had not been to London.

191
00:14:20,639 --> 00:14:23,239
Yes, I suppose you found that out by second sight.

192
00:14:25,139 --> 00:14:27,019
Mrs. Fairfax told me in a letter.

193
00:14:28,540 --> 00:14:30,879
And did she inform you what I went to do?

194
00:14:31,739 --> 00:14:34,919
Oh yes, sir, everybody knew your errand.

195
00:14:36,180 --> 00:14:41,417
You must see the carriage, Jane, and tell me if you don't think it will suit Mrs.

196
00:14:41,417 --> 00:14:45,576
Rochester exactly, and whether she won't look like Queen

197
00:14:45,576 --> 00:14:48,940
Bodicea leaning back against those purple cushions.

198
00:14:50,160 --> 00:14:55,279
I wish, Jane, I were a trifle better adapted to match with her externally.

199
00:14:56,500 --> 00:14:59,779
Tell me now, fairy as you are.

200
00:15:00,580 --> 00:15:02,747
Can't you give me a charm or a filter or

201
00:15:02,747 --> 00:15:05,821
something of that sort to make me a handsome man?

202
00:15:07,040 --> 00:15:11,036
It would be past the power of magic, sir, and in

203
00:15:11,036 --> 00:15:14,819
thought I added, a loving eye is all the charm needed.

204
00:15:15,620 --> 00:15:20,881
To such you are handsome enough, or rather your sternness has a power beyond beauty.

205
00:15:22,480 --> 00:15:26,142
Mr. Rochester had sometimes read my unspoken

206
00:15:26,144 --> 00:15:29,540
thoughts with an acumen to me incomprehensible.

207
00:15:30,239 --> 00:15:36,739
In the present instance, he took no notice of my abrupt vocal response, but he smiled

208
00:15:36,741 --> 00:15:39,194
at me with a certain smile he had of his

209
00:15:39,196 --> 00:15:42,521
own, and which he used but on rare occasions.

210
00:15:43,040 --> 00:15:45,739
He seemed to think it too good for common purposes.

211
00:15:46,779 --> 00:15:48,879
It was the real sunshine of feeling.

212
00:15:49,620 --> 00:15:51,040
He shed it over me now.

213
00:15:52,260 --> 00:15:56,360
Past Janet said he, making room for me to cross the style.

214
00:15:57,339 --> 00:16:02,160
Go up home, and stay your weary little wandering feet at a friend's threshold.

215
00:16:03,220 --> 00:16:09,781
All I had now to do was to obey him in silence, no need for me to colloquize further.

216
00:16:10,019 --> 00:16:13,860
I got over the style without a word, and meant to leave him calmly,

217
00:16:14,360 --> 00:16:18,160
an impulse held me fast, a force turned me round.

218
00:16:18,779 --> 00:16:23,540
I said, or something in me said for me, and in spite of me.

219
00:16:24,500 --> 00:16:27,680
Thank you, Mr. Rochester, for your great kindness.

220
00:16:28,900 --> 00:16:33,540
I'm strangely glad to get back again to you, and wherever you are is my home,

221
00:16:34,319 --> 00:16:35,660
my only home.

222
00:16:37,120 --> 00:16:42,419
I walked on so fast that even he could hardly have overtaken me had he tried.

223
00:16:43,779 --> 00:16:47,019
Little Adele was half wild with delight when she saw me.

224
00:16:48,139 --> 00:16:53,680
Mrs. Fairfax received me with her usual plain friendliness, Leah smiled,

225
00:16:54,279 --> 00:16:57,180
and even Sophie bid me bonsoir with Glee.

226
00:16:58,400 --> 00:16:59,839
This was very pleasant.

227
00:17:00,819 --> 00:17:04,839
There is no happiness like that of being loved by your fellow creatures,

228
00:17:05,919 --> 00:17:09,120
and feeling that your presence is an addition to their comfort.

229
00:17:10,559 --> 00:17:15,279
I, that evening, shot my eyes resolutely against the future.

230
00:17:16,239 --> 00:17:19,440
I stopped my ears against the voice that kept

231
00:17:19,440 --> 00:17:22,821
warning me of near separation and coming grief.

232
00:17:23,300 --> 00:17:29,379
When tea was over, and Mrs. Fairfax had taken her knitting, and I had assumed a

233
00:17:29,381 --> 00:17:35,639
low seat near her, and Adele, kneeling on the carpet, had nestled close up to me,

234
00:17:36,400 --> 00:17:41,180
and a sense of mutual affection seemed to surround us with a ring of golden peace.

235
00:17:42,059 --> 00:17:47,139
I uttered a silent prayer that we might not be parted far or soon.

236
00:17:47,860 --> 00:17:55,199
But when, as we thus sat, Mr. Rochester entered, unannounced, and looking at us,

237
00:17:55,201 --> 00:17:59,360
seemed to take pleasure in the spectacle of a group so amicable.

238
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:04,379
When he said he supposed the old lady was all right now that she had got her adopted

239
00:18:04,381 --> 00:18:07,730
daughter back again, and added that he saw Adele

240
00:18:07,730 --> 00:18:11,341
was pretty croquette sapetitma more on Glee's.

241
00:18:12,080 --> 00:18:17,639
I half ventured to hope that he would, even after his marriage, keep us together

242
00:18:17,641 --> 00:18:21,129
somewhere under the shelter of his protection, and

243
00:18:21,131 --> 00:18:24,019
not quite exiled from the sunshine of his presence.

244
00:18:26,319 --> 00:18:31,559
A fortnight of dubious calm succeeded my return to Thornfield Hall.

245
00:18:33,080 --> 00:18:35,417
Nothing was said of the master's marriage, and

246
00:18:35,417 --> 00:18:38,701
I saw no preparation going on for such an event.

247
00:18:39,239 --> 00:18:44,680
Almost every day, I asked Mrs. Fairfax if she had yet heard anything decided.

248
00:18:45,599 --> 00:18:47,440
Her answer was always in the negative.

249
00:18:49,120 --> 00:18:53,014
Once, she said she had actually put the question to

250
00:18:53,016 --> 00:18:57,059
Mr. Rochester, as to when he was going to bring his bride home.

251
00:18:57,940 --> 00:19:01,930
But he had answered her only by a joke, and one of his

252
00:19:01,932 --> 00:19:05,360
queer looks, and she could not tell what to make of him.

253
00:19:06,680 --> 00:19:10,879
One thing specially surprised me, and that was,

254
00:19:10,881 --> 00:19:14,139
there were no journeyings backward and forward.

255
00:19:15,059 --> 00:19:18,048
No visits to Ingram Park, to be sure it was

256
00:19:18,050 --> 00:19:22,040
20 miles off on the borders of another county.

257
00:19:22,540 --> 00:19:25,500
But what was that distance to an ardent lover?

258
00:19:26,300 --> 00:19:30,006
To so practice and indefatigable a horseman as

259
00:19:30,008 --> 00:19:33,339
Mr. Rochester, it would be but a morning's ride.

260
00:19:34,379 --> 00:19:40,120
I began to cherish hopes I had no right to conceive, that the match was broken off,

261
00:19:40,120 --> 00:19:46,781
that rumour had been mistaken, that one or both parties had changed their minds.

262
00:19:47,360 --> 00:19:51,360
I used to look at my master's face to see if it was sad or fierce.

263
00:19:52,559 --> 00:19:55,317
But I could not remember the time when it had been

264
00:19:55,319 --> 00:19:58,141
so uniformly clear of clouds or evil feelings.

265
00:19:58,879 --> 00:20:03,285
If, in the moments I and my pupil spent with him, I

266
00:20:03,286 --> 00:20:06,959
lacked spirits and sank into inevitable dejection.

267
00:20:07,660 --> 00:20:09,360
He became even gay.

268
00:20:10,120 --> 00:20:15,819
Never had he called me more frequently to his presence, never been kinder to me when

269
00:20:15,821 --> 00:20:21,279
there, and alas, never had I loved him so well.
